expected_issues.description:
Constructor takes `const char * thread_name` but later does `if (thread_name[0] != '\0') ...`. If caller passes nullptr this is UB. Either require non-null explicitly (e.g., `chassert(thread_name)` / document contract) or safely handle null by checking `thread_name && thread_name[0] != '\0'` (and use a fallback like "" in exception messages).

```suggestion
        if (thread_name && thread_name[0] != '\0')
            setThreadName(thread_name);
```

